   - Creation: BeginTrace stores owner/config at +0x480..+0x4A8; CreateActiveTrace allocates a0x10
   controller plus0xF8 state and spawns ALuxTraceMeshActor; callers publish the pair into
   prepared+418 or child+428.
   - Ownership: +418 prepared strong pairs, +428 child strong pairs, +3E0 active/fading weak pairs,
   +3F0 VFX-completion weak pairs, +400 deferred VFX-registration weak pairs. These are arrays, not
   hash ownership.
   - Active entry: +0x50 is flSourceScale; +0xA0 is cached trace state; +0xA8 is its reference
   controller.
   - Tick: lifetimes, fade samples, retained spline history, actor state, dirty flags, async work,
   removals, refcounts, and callbacks advance here and in the two child update routes.
   - Completion: +0x438 is the finished/inactive latch. Native trace code initializes +0x460/+0x468
   to null and no reflected TraceFinished route exists; process admission must prove the pair stays
   null or restore the one-shot callback transactionally.
   - Release/recreation: ALuxTraceManager_ReleaseEffectComponent destroys manager +0x3A8 and clears
   it; later registration can create a different component/actor generation.
   
   Rollback Relevance:
   Both material/fade and spline/interpolator update routes mutate retained simulation state and
   shared-reference ownership. They must execute during every rollback resimulation pass. The
   completion callback is source-ordered after all those mutations and dependent-VFX registration.
   Only proven downstream visual terminals such as SetLuxTraceMeshMaterialScalar may be journaled;
   their state-producing callers may not be skipped, deferred, or stripped.
   
