   pCompletionEventReference: address of the graph task's completion pointer at task +40.
   
   Returns
   -------
   void. Clears the scheduled-task binding after the callback or when disabled.
   
   Algorithm
   ---------
   1. If payload +20/+21 are set, visit prerequisite entries for diagnostics.
   2. If function +D is enabled, derive interval delta from world +930 or +934.
   3. Invoke tick-function vtable +8 with function, delta, level tick, thread, and completion
   reference.
   4. Clear tick-function +18 only after its callback returns.
   
   Structure Layout
   ----------------
   Tick function +C: flags; bit0 chooses world +934 instead of +930.
   +D: enabled state; +18: scheduled task binding.
   +20/+28: prerequisite array/count; +3C: previous time; +40: tick interval.
   Payload +20/+21: prerequisite diagnostic flags.
   
   Replay ownership
   ----------------
   The virtual callback can reach the BattleManager executor. Clearing +18 is pending work
   after an interior yield. Caller 14215ED20 subsequently completes and recycles the task.
   
   Special Cases
   -------------
   llTickFunctionOrPrerequisite is a merged register, not a proven single struct pointer.
   A register-only lVar1 can reappear after SSA regeneration; same pointer-role limitation.
   Completion-event storage remains generic until its full task-graph contract is audited.
   
